{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2225 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a18bebcd71236013bfed195e8fd7d39d3a7e6502071929a7a3528b38f3a01928" :edb/db-before-t 2224 :edb/db-after-t 2225 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535537 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:03:30.242Z" 13194139535537 true] [17592186228128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354281 13194139535537 true] [17592186228128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354282 13194139535537 true] [17592186228128 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354282 13194139535537 true] [17592186229108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354260 13194139535537 true] [17592186229108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354267 13194139535537 true] [17592186229108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354274 13194139535537 true] [17592186229109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354283 13194139535537 true] [17592186229614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535537 true] [17592186229614 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nConsider the following initial value problem:\n$y^{′} = x^{2} + y^{3}, y(1) =-1.4$\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2)$. Round your answer to two decimal places.$y(2) \\approx$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535537 false] [17592186229614 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+{y}^{3},\\,y(1)=-1.4\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186229614 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})+({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+y-{y}_{\\text{new}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+y-{y}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\n Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5(1)^{2}+0.5(-1.4)^{3}+0.5(2)^{2}-1.4-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5-1.372+2-1.4-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.272.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=-1.4$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}.\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=1.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{3}-({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-0.272}{1.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1)=-1.4,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =-1.4 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & ≈-1.274\\,227 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈-1.251\\,778 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈-1.251\\,069\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-1.25,$ rounded to two decimal places." 13194139535537 true] [17592186354260 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354261 13194139535537 true] [17592186354260 1089 "q-334072" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354260 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535537 true] [17592186354260 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=6\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current values $x$ and $y?$" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354260 1113 #uuid "872582af-4f14-53f7-9ee8-179fc32d0c45" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354260 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(6\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}+6\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}+3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}+3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{{{y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354262 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354263 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354264 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354265 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354266 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1041 "selection" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354266 13194139535537 true] [17592186354261 1110 #uuid "067f8362-bbc5-529d-af2a-79c89a8a70b5" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354262 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}^{2}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354262 1111 #uuid "383a9302-0349-5654-8bdc-e0e464d1c568" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354263 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354263 1111 #uuid "6f95f36e-2cf1-571c-9514-fa59a20b08ea" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354264 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{3}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354264 1111 #uuid "1e33e08a-3d11-5267-91f1-7d3ddd583be3" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354265 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-6\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-6\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354265 1111 #uuid "4e5f3592-8fd4-5bc5-950c-dfa6fd085f05" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354266 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354266 1111 #uuid "9ca2e251-88f2-5c8b-9d5e-f815c2edd54f" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354267 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354268 13194139535537 true] [17592186354267 1089 "q-334077" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354267 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535537 true] [17592186354267 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}\\sqrt{y},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354267 1113 #uuid "c3e7b77a-8724-5c98-839a-9b13b32a04b2" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354267 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354269 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354270 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354271 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354272 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354273 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1041 "selection" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354272 13194139535537 true] [17592186354268 1110 #uuid "4c6533f3-0198-5a41-a1ef-b0cf440a7dca" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354269 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354269 1111 #uuid "4c9d1d96-6f3c-5fd9-b43c-a44e3683e9d8" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354270 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354270 1111 #uuid "5f1e0ced-9569-5168-b33f-f29d7cf19154" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354271 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354271 1111 #uuid "338b4665-3a5e-5508-b6f0-a7bfe1198443" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354272 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354272 1111 #uuid "4a90a6e4-0ed4-5807-85a2-cad515a8a9ed" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354273 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-2" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354273 1111 #uuid "285e2475-4b47-5219-8a94-024f5eccbe15" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354274 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354275 13194139535537 true] [17592186354274 1089 "q-334080" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354274 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535537 true] [17592186354274 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-y,\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354274 1113 #uuid "27c9463d-3427-5712-975e-bf5711e6e029" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354274 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example  $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({x}^{2}-y)+({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}).\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2}-1+{2}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}(0+4-{y}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354276 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354277 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354278 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354279 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354280 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1041 "selection" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354280 13194139535537 true] [17592186354275 1110 #uuid "22c64eb7-5d70-57e1-b5c4-62cddb992905" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354276 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-2" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535537 true] [17592186354276 1111 #uuid "56d5e153-950c-5595-ae6c-15d9ec062d12" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354277 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-4" 13194139535537 true] [17592186354277 1103 #edb/ref 175921